1. setup first VLANS, port Assigning, trunking with NAtive trunk 100
2. Router DHCP, CME for Telephony Services
3. very important note always use no shut just to make sure and spanning-tree portfast

1. VLANS in All Switches
conf t
vlan 10
name MANAGEMENT
vlan 20
name FINANCE
vlan 30
name HR
vlan 70
name VOICE
vlan 100
name Native-Trunking

2. port assigning for designated VLANS
conf t
int port# / range port#
swithcport mode access
switchport access vlan #

!! phone assigning
switchport voice vlan #

3. Trunking all switches with designated vlans
conf t
int port#
switchport mode trunk !if error in encapsulation use the 2nd line
switchport trunk encapsulation dot1q
!repeat the line 1
switchport trunk native vlan # !! if not use the default native vlan
!!import note: if no using the native vlan no need to use command native vlan #
switchport trunk allowed vlan # !!(use vlan# - vlan #) for shortcut ranges

4. Create a SVI and DHCP using the router
!!in Router DHCP
conf t
int port#.vlandId#
encapsulation dot1q vlanId#
ip address x.x.x.x subnetmask
exit
ip dhcp excluded-address x.x.x.x x.x.x.x !!optional
ip dhcp pool Name
network x.x.x.x subnetmask
default-router SVI IP
dns-server 8.8.8.8
domain-name NAME

!for DHCP of Telephone
ip dhcp pool Name
network x.x.x.x subnetmask
default-router SVI IP
option 150 ip ipAddress of CME-Router
dns-server 8.8.8.8
domain-name NAME

5. FOR CME ROuter Telephony Setup
conf t
int port#
no shut
ip address x.x.x.x subnetmask

!!For setup telephony service
conf t
telephony-service
max-ephones # (1-40)
max-dn # (1-20)
ip source-address CME-Router_Ip port 2000
auto assign # to # (1-40)
create cnf_files

!extensions
ephone-dn #
number #

6. Link the Coreswitch to the CME-Router for access Voice VLAN using port assigning in Coreswitch
conf t
int port #
switchport mode access
switchport access vlan (the Voice vlan #)
spanning-tree portfast
no shut

